==Trivia==
*Everlord is not an actual word. It is likely a pun on ''ever'' (at all times; always) and ''overlord''.
*The name Wanwan is derived from ワン ''wan'', the Japanese onomatopoeia for a dog's bark.
*Wanwan's Japanese name, Pero (ペロ), may be derived from the Spanish word ''perro'' (dog), possibly due to chihuahuas originating in Mexico.
*Among the Tier 2 [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], Everlord Wanwan appears to represent the virtue of kindness, as his description implies he speaks very kindly to those he captivates.
*He can be seen as a foil to [[King Wahwah]]. Wahwah rose to power through efforts and tribulations whereas Everlord Wanwan got famous from a reality TV show. King Wahwah is even upset that his TV star brother is more popular.
*The combined Enemy Guide descriptions of King Wahwah, Everlord Wanwan, and [[Mistress Celeboodle]] imply that the little brother mentioned in Wahwah's description is Wanwan, which is not only because Wanwan is a variant of Wahwah but also because Mistress Celeboodle's description states that she married a chihuahua reality TV "star". This also leads to Wahwah being Mistress Celeboodle's brother-in-law.
**This is confirmed in King Wahwah's Japanese description, which directly states that Wanwan is his brother. Interestingly, this was before Wanwan was added to the game.
*He has the longest warp distance and warp duration of all enemies.

